<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Vista Butte from Swampy Lakes Sno-Park</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:273-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="43.989467" lon="-121.568160"><ele>1769.6</ele><name>Swampy Lakes Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead th:swampy-lakes-sno-park (OSM relation 11960476); confidence: high; pdf_page: 273; book_elev_ft: 5700; quote: map 62: SWAMPY LAKES SNO-PARK 5700'</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.995480" lon="-121.579150"><ele>1813.3</ele><name>Swampy Lakes Trail / Ridge Loop junction</name><desc>source: OSM: west end of Ridge Loop way 286208544 beside the start of Swampy Lakes Trail #23 way 279479053; confidence: high; pdf_page: 274; quote: ski the Swampy Lakes Trail toward the Swampy Lakes Shelter, and in 0.8 mile turn left onto the Ridge Loop</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.994180" lon="-121.591460"><ele>1872.9</ele><name>Ridge Loop / Butte Trail junction (6120')</name><desc>source: OSM: Ridge Loop way 286208544 meets Swampy-Dutchman Trail #40 (piste:name Butte Trail) way 91883634; confidence: high; pdf_page: 273; book_elev_ft: 6120; quote: map 62: 6120' at the Ridge Loop / Vista Butte Trail junction, 0.6 from the turn</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.993590" lon="-121.603570"><ele>1938.1</ele><name>Bruce's Ball Park</name><desc>source: OSM: Vista Butte Trail #40.2 (way 299952087) leaves the Butte Trail; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 276; quote: climbs to the Butte Trail, following it to Bruce's Ball Park, where the side trail to the summit goes to the left</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.992055" lon="-121.598381"><ele>2016.1</ele><name>Vista Butte summit</name><desc>source: OSM node 3040323668 Vista Butte; confidence: high; pdf_page: 275; book_elev_ft: 6619; quote: The summit of the 6,619-foot butte ... is a wide, windy snow ridge</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Vista Butte from Swampy Lakes Sno-Park</name><desc>1. Swampy Lakes Sno-Park -&gt; Swampy Lakes Trail / Ridge Loop junction: osm (medium), 0.84 mi | 2. Swampy Lakes Trail / Ridge Loop junction -&gt; Ridge Loop / Butte Trail junction (6120'): osm (high), 0.70 mi | 3. Ridge Loop / Butte Trail junction (6120') -&gt; Bruce's Ball Park: osm (high), 0.89 mi | 4. Bruce's Ball Park -&gt; Vista Butte summit: osm (high), 0.50 mi</desc>
